{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingResidualExponent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingResidualExponent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent_five","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**The empirical law.** At the measured per-unit weight `w = 5`, the residual exponent is the\nobserved `10A − 5 = 5(2A − 1)`. The `2A−1` is derived; only the `5` is empirical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent_eq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L66-L70","doc":"**Chain-topology decomposition.** The residual exponent is `w·(2A − 1)` — `w` for each of the\n`A` nucleons and each of the `A−1` bonds. This is the derived combinatorial content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.residualExponent","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The residual exponent under per-unit weight `w`: `w` for each nucleon and each bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.interface_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.interface_crossings","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L58-L61","doc":"**The interface crossings are exactly the bonds.** `len(W_atom) − len(W_free) = A − 1`,\nmatching the chain's `A−1` consecutive-pair interfaces (verified on D/T/³He/⁴He/⁶Li: +1/+2/+2/+3/+5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.wAtomLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.wAtomLen","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L55-L56","doc":"`W_atom` crossing count: the constituents plus one interface crossing per bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.wFreeLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.wFreeLen","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L52-L53","doc":"`W_free` crossing count: 11 per nucleon (`g0`:7 + `g1`:4), interfaces dropped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.chainUnits_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.chainUnits_eq","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The chain has `2A − 1` topological units (`A` nucleons + `A−1` bonds). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.chainUnits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.chainUnits","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L45-L46","doc":"Chain topological units = nucleons + bonds (`= 2A − 1` for `A ≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.bonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.bonds","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Number of interface bonds in the `A`-nucleon chain (`A ≥ 1`): one per consecutive pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.nucleons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Binding.ResidualExponent.nucleons","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingResidualExponent.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Number of nucleons in the chain (`A = Z + N`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}